{"id": "section-body-12299", "title": "Lower Abdominal Pain Syndrome or Pelvic Inflammatory Disease (PID)", "chapterId": "chapter-twelve", "blocks": [{"id": "body-12299", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Lower Abdominal Pain Syndrome or Pelvic Inflammatory Disease (PID)", "runs": [{"text": "Lower"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Abdominal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Pain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Syndrome"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Pelvic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Inflammatory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Disease"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PID)"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1397"}}, {"id": "body-12300", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "PID is defined as the inflammation of the uterus, fallopian tubes, ovaries and pelvic peritoneum. It is also known as lower abdominal pain syndrome. It commonly occurs as a result of infection ascending from the cervix. It can also occur as a result of trans-cervical procedure. Mainly caused by Neisseria gonorrhoeae, Chlamydia trachomatis and Anaerobic bacteria", "runs": [{"text": "PID is defined as the inflammation of the uterus, fallopian tubes, ovaries and pelvic peritoneum. It is also known as lower abdominal pain syndrome. It commonly occurs as a result of infection ascending from the cervix. It can also occur as a result of trans-cervical procedure. Mainly caused by "}, {"text": "Neisseria", "italic": true}, {"text": " ", "italic": true}, {"text": "gonorrhoeae, Chlamydia", "italic": true}, {"text": " ", "italic": true}, {"text": "trachomatis", "italic": true}, {"text": " ", "italic": true}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Anaerobic bacteria"}]}, {"id": "body-12302", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-12303", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Lower abdominal pain and tenderness, Painful micturition, Painful coitus, Abnormal vaginal discharge, Menometrorrhagia, fever and sometimes nausea and vomiting.", "runs": [{"text": "Lower"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "abdominal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tenderness,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Painful"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "micturition,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Painful"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "coitus,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Abnormal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vaginal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "discharge,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Menometrorrhagia,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fever and sometimes nausea and vomiting."}]}, {"id": "body-12304-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Note", "runs": [{"text": "Note", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-12304-textbox1-00002", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Delayed or inadequately treated PID may lead to chronic lower abdominal pain,", "runs": [{"text": "Delayed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inadequately"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "treated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "PID"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lead"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chronic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lower"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "abdominal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pain,"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1389"}}, {"id": "body-12304-textbox1-00003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Pelvic abscess,", "runs": [{"text": "Pelvic abscess,"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1389"}}, {"id": "body-12304-textbox1-00004", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Ectopic pregnancy,", "runs": [{"text": "Ectopic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pregnancy,"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1389"}}, {"id": "body-12304-textbox1-00005", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Dysmenorrhea and infertility.", "runs": [{"text": "Dysmenorrhea and"}